{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/242377-perceiving-infrastructure","id":242377,"title":"Perceiving Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-27T12:07:55-07:00","id":242377,"title":"Perceiving Infrastructure","content":"No &quot;system&quot; is listed under the section &quot;Perceiving Infrastructure&quot; (Demon the Descent p. 183). Does this mean that a Demon automatically sees infrastructure for what it is somehow? Do they know what it does? How does this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T12:36:06-07:00","id":242422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who survive learn to keep a constant, vigilant watch for signs that angels have found them. They have one great advantage over their new human neighbors in keeping out of the way \u2014 they\u2019re still angelic enough that none of the mind tricks, illusions and spatial folding the God-Machine uses to conceal its facilities work on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p235</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Demon , techgnosis \u2014 insight into technology \u2014 describes the God-Machine and the way it lurks, hidden and unnoticed, around the corners and under the skin of the human world. Demons can sense all the different forms of Infrastructure, can always see facilities and gears, and can sense angels through aetheric resonance or by risking being sensed in return. Thanks to their ability to perceive the God-Machine\u2019s work, demons can even feel the build-up of energies when an occult matrix forms in Infrastructure.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Demons are inherently aware when something has techgnostic meaning, but they don\u2019t have the ability to instantly know what that meaning <i>is.</i> Without the connection to the God-Machine they lost in the Fall, they can sense when their creator is enacting a plan, but have to guess at what the plan or its objective is, risk doing nothing with the possibility that the plan is directed at them, or investigate further. Which is where the second theme of the game \u2014 espionage \u2014 comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">characterlimit</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T13:00:06-07:00","id":242490,"title":"","content":"Got. it. They notice it automatically, but that doesn't give them any information about what it is. They also have to ACT like they don't see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T13:16:32-07:00","id":242496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/242377-perceiving-infrastructure?p=242490#post242490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got. it. They notice it automatically, but that doesn't give them any information about what it is. They also have to ACT like they don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, considering the way the Poker Face works, is definitely really easy for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T16:43:41-07:00","id":244405,"title":"","content":"I've wondered how this shakes out in practical terms, in say a city or something. It would seem like this would present an awesome amount of information. I've been assuming that a typical city is largely stuffed to the gills with infrastructure, with tens of thousands of occult matrixi being formed at any given time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T17:20:07-07:00","id":244421,"title":"","content":"Yes. Also, a lot of the stories and bits describe seeing the horrific gears and mechanisms of an Infrastructure. I assume these would be fully visible. Does EVERY infrastructure have a place like this? If so, where is it? Is it related to the Linchpin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T21:56:28-07:00","id":244533,"title":"","content":"I think the Gears are as often metaphorical as they are literal.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you can actually physically see gears in a lot of Infrastructure, but I don't imagine it's a hard requirement that they be present.<br /> <br /> They're a useful shorthand for &quot;Here be God-Machine weirdness&quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T11:14:52-07:00","id":244897,"title":"","content":"I've never actually used literal gears, but they do describe them, so I suppose I'm being unauthentic. I generally speaking try avoid using folded space as well ; I view it as being 'expensive', roughly equal in terms of God Machine resources to wiring up an office with a heavy internet backbone, an expense that's not altogether worth it except in specific places. Most infrastructure is mundane enough so that if you stumbled into it as a human it'd be weird, and confusing (why on earth do they need 4 janitors for one floor?) but not overtly impossible.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the vast majority of it is empty I propose. On my 'Random Infrastructure' table (which I find I need, because CONSTANTLY people are looking for more of it for whatever story reason), I propose that eighty percent of it is simply lying around empty. Not in active use, not really important. Just... waiting, or dead, depending on what you interpret it as when you find it. These sort of places are best for converting into boltholes if you are reasonably convinced they've fallen off the grid or won't be bothered for a while.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:16:53-07:00","id":245131,"title":"","content":"MissMaddy can you share or talk about your random infrastructure table?<br /> <br /> How often do they find bits of infrastructure hanging around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T23:02:43-07:00","id":245198,"title":"","content":"Sure, it's pretty simple.<br /> <br /> Roughly twenty percent of human structures have some sort of recognizably 'God Machine' infrastructure I've proposed, which implies a kind of weird nWoD which we're comfortable with. Only a quarter of these are 'active'. Active does not imply they are inhabited - they may be being used for storage, or simply currently empty. A quarter of the active infrastructure is in current use.<br /> <br /> So, 20% of human structures house some sort of infrastructure. ( IE : A broken down factory with huge water damage, broken windows, and rats )<br /> Of that, 25% is 'active' - considered to be a current, usable resource, rather than abandoned. ( IE : An empty garage, a safehouse with nobody in it )<br /> Of that, 25% is being used RIGHT NOW - implying personnel, additional security, and story seeds. ( IE : People. Possibly angels. Who knows? )<br /> <br /> We like to use this in tandem with Google Earth. So, when we're trying to determine where infrastructure is on our street we can zoom in with the nice 3d buildings and mark them. We just point to a building and roll a few percentiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 08-31-2014, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:29:38-07:00","id":245341,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T21:18:21-07:00","id":247431,"title":"","content":"Remember when you play Silent Hill and before something supernatural and scary happen the radio goes static and the noise makes it even scarier?<br /> <br /> I use the description of the gears the same way, starting slowly with just ordinary gears and as closer as the demon gets to the linchpin weird things happen. The gears get alien features, something organic such as tubes filled with blood or metalic organs filled with some white oil shining like aether as well. Laterns shine brighter and phones lose the network.<br /> <br /> I get creepier as they get closer. I wanna them to feel disgusted as they would hate to be reminded of how was being an angel and also wanna introduce this fear that they could be captured at any time while they risk interacting with an infrastructure. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T14:27:40-07:00","id":249168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/242377-perceiving-infrastructure?p=242490#post242490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got. it. They notice it automatically, but that doesn't give them any information about what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but...<br /> <br /> Does Infrastructure specifically stand out to the Fallen? Or do they need to actively look for it? Will Infrastructure always be clearly visible to the Demons wherever it is? Is it possible that they're ever mistaken about seeing a piece of Infrastructure? Would it work like how an artist always sees the architectural elements of buildings downtown? Or is it more like seeing an English word in the neon signs lighting a Japanese city? Would a mundane wall or slab of concrete suffice to hide Infrastructure from the eyes of a Fallen Angel of the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> Part of me knows that the above questions represent pieces of the game that ought to be decided upon by the Storyteller, but the experience of identifying Infrastructure remains maddeningly vague for me, even with the info that <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Satchel</span></b> so kindly pointed out (srsly mate, thank you for that). Until I have a handle on how that works, I'm proper scared of attempting to run this game for my troupe. The idea of my players' character wandering around the city and just pointing out Infrastructure the way I point out faux-Victorian columns doesn't bode well for me keeping much mystery in the game.<br /> <br /> Yeah, like I said, I COULD decide on how this works on my own, but I kinda think that the book ought to give me some more direction than it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:55:09-07:00","id":249368,"title":"","content":"Found one more that I'd been looking for and missed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p243</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Facilities may be cloaked, have limited access points, or both. Facilities that warp time and space might only be accessed by specific doors at specific times\u2014a hidden button in an elevator at midnight, a security door in an alleyway, a mysterious hatch built into the floor of city hall\u2019s basement. Demons can see facilities when they\u2019re \u201conly\u201d invisible and sense that something\u2019s wrong when they\u2019re near the access points of dimensionally-transcendent ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, for good measure:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p184</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can feel Aether through a sensation dubbed \u201caetheric resonance.\u201d The specifics of the feeling vary from demon to demon, to some it is like static, a slow uncomfortable pull, while others describe Aether as possessing a metallic scent or strange hue. <b>All of the God-Machine\u2019s most potent endeavors are dependent upon the conversion of Essence into Aether.</b> Angelic Numina, Influences, Manifestations and true forms, as well as facilities and stockpiles: everything emits Aether. Aetheric resonance serves as a valuable asset by which the Unchained may feel out the workings of their enemy.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Being in a Twilight state does not protect an angel from aetheric resonance, but demons hidden by Cover and angels masked by Infrastructure are not immediately revealed. This defense lapses only briefly when they expend Aether or Essence. <b>Facilities register with particular intensity, thus the God-Machine frequently employs special masking devices, Aether-eating cryptids, and other oddities to hide its most critical projects.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:45:44-07:00","id":249438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/242377-perceiving-infrastructure?p=249168#post249168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>The following answers are not canonical, but I have used them functionally, so maybe they'll be useful to you!<br /> <br /> <b>Does Infrastructure specifically stand out to the Fallen? </b><br /> <br /> Yes. Fallen can detect any infrastructure at a glance. However, because nearly anything you can imagine is in some way infrastructure, the practical utility of this ability is not particularly important.<br /> <br /> <b>Or do they need to actively look for it? </b><br /> <br /> No. The ability to see it is passive, like another spectrum of light.<br /> <br /> <b>Will Infrastructure always be clearly visible to the Demons wherever it is? </b><br /> <br /> No. Demons must 'see' something to identify it as Infrastructure UNLESS it is being used in some way ; active use / activation can cause 'vibrations' and 'signals' which can carry through solid objects and over long distances on a case by case basis. The bigger the matrix, usually, the more profound the disturbance.<br /> <br /> <b>Is it possible that they're ever mistaken about seeing a piece of Infrastructure? </b><br /> <br /> No. You might suggest that some device could mimic infrastructure as a God Machine trap, but that device itself would by definition be infrastructure oddly enough so it's not really a trick.<br /> <br /> <b>Would it work like how an artist always sees the architectural elements of buildings downtown? </b><br /> <br /> Not exactly ; it's more just another 'sense', another organ along with eyes and nose.<br /> <br /> <b>Or is it more like seeing an English word in the neon signs lighting a Japanese city?</b><br /> <br /> Not sure what's meant here, sorry!<br /> <br /> <b>Would a mundane wall or slab of concrete suffice to hide Infrastructure from the eyes of a Fallen Angel of the God-Machine?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, unless the Infrastructure was active. If it was active, it might produce waste heat (Aether), vibrations or signals which might be noticed. The ease with which one might notice these things is dependent on the context of the infrastructure (and matrix) in question.<br /> <br /> <b>The idea of my players' character wandering around the city and just pointing out Infrastructure the way I point out faux-Victorian columns doesn't bode well for me keeping much mystery...</b><br /> <br /> Understandable. Infrastructure is built and maintained by humans as well as the God Machine, so you're not going to bother to describe most of it as it would be reduntant. Most of it remains unused in potentia until the God Machine stirs and makes use of it in some project or another, like an orchard with many unpicked peaches. The modern world is a garden of plenty for the industrious matrix-monster.<br /> <br /> That said, Players will end up paying much more notice to active infrastructure, which is when infrastructure being used to currently produce a matrix of some sort. Because demons can intuitively sense this 'charge' and how it 'builds' (depending on the unique context of the situation), this is how infrastructure sense is useful in a practical way. Identifying a door is infrastructure isn't particularly useful because -every- door is infrastructure. However, identifying that it is slowly charging up and at 12:05 is going to discharge something... which implies the God Machine is using it in some way... that's going to merit significantly more attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T09:16:14-07:00","id":250801,"title":"","content":"Hey, thanks a lot <b><span style=\"color:#008080\">MissMaddy</span></b>!<br /> <br /> The problem I have with these rules is three-fold: First, I only use the PDF version of <b>Demon: the Descent</b> rather than a physical copy that I'd, you know, physically bookmark and whatnot; second, as <b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Satchel</span></b>'s comments show, the rules for these are not all in one place in the book; and third is that the book's index is imprecise about these rules. I've noticed a similar trend with <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> 2d ed. (a/k/a <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, which has no index at all) and <b>Mummy: the Curse</b>, but the former's awesomeness got me to buy the physical book, and the latter isn't nearly as interesting to me as <b>Demon: the Descent</b>. I'm saving my pennies for a physical copy of <b>Demon</b>, but your help shall suffice until I get it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T16:07:25-07:00","id":251120,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine often also masks infrastructure with Line-Of-Sight. For example: The infrastructure in a building is it's broom closet, but not the entire building itself, and therefore cannot be seen from outside the building but only when able to -see- the broom closet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}